 Democracy, established on November 8, 1999, in Bratislava, Slovakia, is a political party that has played a pivotal role in shaping contemporary Slovak political landscape. It emerged during a period of significant transformation in Eastern Europe following the collapse of communism, reflecting the region's shift towards democratic governance and social welfare. The party, often abbreviated as Smer, was founded by Robert Fico, who became its prominent leader and a significant figure in Slovak politics, influencing both domestic and regional policies.

